able to offer for sale at a given price during a given period of time.
Stock refers to total quantity of a particular commodity that is
available with the firm at a particular point of time.
2. Supply is a flow concept as it relates to a period of time. Stock is not a flow concept as it relates to a particular point of
time.
3. Supply is always related to price of the commodity as it changes
with change in price.
Stock is not related to price of the commodity as it indicates a
fixed quantity.
